        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "OUT (pin 7) feeds the heater connector J6 pin 2"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "An external device connected to J5 can short GPIO1 to GND or inject a signal, overriding or damaging the MCU and causing unintended heater activation or failure.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain an extra screw terminal J5 connected directly to the ESP32 GPIO1 heater control net, which is not present in the specification and creates a risk of shorting or overriding the heater control signal."
}

